      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1178,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical substance with the chemical formula **$H_2O$**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what makes water unique and important:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\nWater is a **polar molecule**. Because oxygen is more \"thirsty\" for electrons than hydrogen, the oxygen atom pulls the shared electrons toward itself. This creates a slight negative charge on the oxygen side and a slight positive charge on the hydrogen side. This polarity is what allows water to stick to itself (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion).\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is one of the few substances on Earth that naturally exists as a solid, a liquid, and a gas at temperatures commonly found on the planet.\n*   **Solid:** Ice (frozen water).\n*   **Liquid:** The form we drink and use for washing.\n*   **Gas:** Water vapor (invisible gas in the air).\n\n### 3. Unique Physical Properties\nWater has several properties that make it essential for life:\n*   **Universal Solvent:** Water is excellent at dissolving other substances. This is why it is the main transport system in plants and animals, moving nutrients and waste around the body.\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick together very strongly at the surface, creating a kind of \"skin.\" This allows small insects to walk on water.\n*   **High Specific Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps the temperature of the human body stable.\n\n### 4. Abundance\nWater is the most abundant compound on the surface of the Earth. It covers about 71% of the planet and makes up about 60% of the human body. Without water, life as we know it would not exist."
